workplan/pipeline-state-graph/IDEAL-GRAPH.md:1:# Ideal pipeline graph: the least structure that meets the project's conditions
workplan/pipeline-state-graph/IDEAL-GRAPH.md:11:O1 "create an idealized new state graph that has as little infrastructure and code as possible that still meets all conditions required of project for a walkable pipeline all directions that can dynamically scrape mine organize and sort all relevant information from any source for any parameter regardless of search slug" · O2 "ideal state graph just be code architecture compliant" (read as "must") · O3 "wherever there is a conflict, adjudicate to ensure 100% accuracy, code compliance and logic for ensuring walkability in pipeline as well as dynamic information collection" · O4 "ensure that you strive to minimize amount of code so that it is as distilled and clean as possible as well as deduplicating and reconciling all conflicts" · O5 "centralized where possible and rely on pointers and injectable code" · O6 "the less hard coded, the better" · O7 "we need to ensure handshakes both top-down and bottom-up, and we need to ensure walkability across all tables with references and ids" · O8 "handshake ALL directions".
workplan/pipeline-state-graph/IDEAL-GRAPH.md:17:A condition is a requirement an active ruling, the mission, a governance contract or one of the four owner capabilities imposes. Every object in §3 cites the conditions it serves; an object with none is not in the ideal.
workplan/pipeline-state-graph/IDEAL-GRAPH.md:44:- **K26** Best-practice synthesis prose is authored only at the Opus/Fable floor. LED-061, CLM-041, PIP-22.
