workplan/pipeline-state-graph/RULINGS.md:137:PREMISES: EVI-049/052/055 (tier-system §8, owner directive 2026-07-20). DR-2026-07-21 Option A `:44` "State machine unchanged"; `:47-51` band at determination level (owner directive, later). EVI-325/326/338, LED-010, PIP-03 (methodology 2.2: T3-grey alone → pending; single T6 → pending). Engine: `scripts/assess/assess_cell.py:1436-1438` (T3-grey → pending), `:1432-1434` (regulatory below richness → pending), `:1510` (regulatory at richness → provisional); P-ENG-T3 PASS. IDEAL-GRAPH §12 Q1 recommends provisional at ○.
workplan/pipeline-state-graph/RULINGS.md:139:RULING: Band only. The engine stands; the ideal's change is a doctrine change not adopted. C-003 is a wording repair: "anchors" in EVI-052 and MIS-04 names the band; MIS-04's "stated = ≥Tier 3" is stale against EVI-325 (owner merge).
workplan/pipeline-state-graph/RULINGS.md:143:PREMISES: LED-018 (2026-07-13); LED-013/014, EVI-058/094 (Option A, owner directive 2026-07-21); EVI-241 (anchored cells: floor value never "best practice"); EVI-394 (methodology 3.4 bare "Code requires…") against EVI-194/229/230 (flag binds every rendering); `status_corrections` entry for LED-018.
workplan/pipeline-state-graph/RULINGS.md:206:PREMISES: OPI-229 (reasoning doc manual; survives in part per C-040). LED-151/152 (owner 2026-09-09: "you have to compute it. I can't handle this load manually"). `convergence_assessment` (5 rows) holds the synthesis narrative and the divergence lists MIS-06 requires. `reasoning_doc_citations` 0 rows; `promoted_to_rdc_id` NULL on 101/101; `references/bpc-reasoning/` = `_template.md` + one file; `bpc_metadata` 0 rows; `validate_bpc` blocking, basis `hygiene`, named by no criterion; `nine-step-synthesis` → `validate_reasoning` advisory red; `pre_rehab_banner_audit` quarantined. CLAUDE.md §6 "Only Opus-class models write `best_practice_synthesis`" is routing, not a deliverable.
workplan/pipeline-state-graph/RULINGS.md:305:**R43 Searches without a slug.** `search_executions.slug` and `search_candidates.found_under_slug` become nullable, and `search_executions` gains a nullable `parameter_id → base_parameters`; a CHECK requires that a search says what it is for: `COALESCE(slug, parameter_id, mined_ref_id) IS NOT NULL`. PREMISES: the owner's "any parameter regardless of search slug" (`main.jsonl:4583`); "while we search by slug, we scan each source for any and all applicable parameters" and the scan contract (LED-195/196/201: slugs guide search only); R18's lens keys are already independent of the slug; 2 of 106 slugs have ever been searched; the key of a determination is parameter × lens, so a parameter-targeted search with no slug has nowhere to say which parameter it was for; `IDEAL-GRAPH.md` (lines 225 and 236) drafts the same shape with a `synthesis_id` that the live schema does not have. INFERENCE: a mandatory slug makes the search record a second filter on a pipeline whose method is slug-free, and the walk parameter → searches has no pointer today (`WALKABILITY.md` §7, finding 4). RULING: build it as one table-rebuild migration for the two tables by the 081 procedure (inbound keys from `search_candidates`, `search_admissions`, `search_execution_artefacts`; views `v_coverage_*`, `v_source_admission`, `v_coverage_lens` dropped and recreated verbatim; `AFTER_DATA` marker; `sqlite_sequence` saved and restored), after R18 and in its own tooling PR; `log-search` accepts no slug when `--parameter` or `--mining` is given and refuses a search that names none; `search_candidates.found_under_slug` keeps its column (data migrations INSERT it: rule 5). Not rehearsed: the plan's Phase 3 research row makes the rehearsal its first act. OVERTURN: the rehearsal shows a reader that cannot tolerate a NULL slug that the sweep did not find.
