workplan/pipeline-state-graph/rehearsals/B-r14-rename.md:223:## Step 6: walkability (the IDEAL-GRAPH §6 script)
workplan/pipeline-state-graph/rehearsals/C-r7-tier-marker.md:40:| `c47620c` | migration `102_specification_marker.sql`: ADD COLUMN `marker` with 2 CHECKs, and `v_best_practice` redefined without `strength_band`. Engine computes and writes the marker; `EvidenceStateRecord.marker`; 4 tests fixed; marker cases added | 7 | +167/−33 |
workplan/pipeline-state-graph/rehearsals/C-r7-tier-marker.md:95:- No view or trigger reads `v_best_practice`.
workplan/pipeline-state-graph/rehearsals/C-r7-tier-marker.md:171:> - **View.** It redefines `v_best_practice` without `strength_band`, a second two-valued band that reads `anchored` over a ○ proxy cell and has no code reader.
workplan/pipeline-state-graph/rehearsals/C-r7-tier-marker.md:181:> The marker is the engine's output and has one home, `specifications.marker` (specification row). `v_best_practice` carries it through `SELECT *`, and the one view to be built reads it, so the band half of the register invariants holds by construction: the CHECK refuses a regulatory-stratum-only row above ○ and a live stated or provisional row without a marker. What the renderer still owns is the weak/code-derived flag text and the register map, plus rendering `provisional ●` (T3-clinical-only, or an H4-capped cell) distinctly from `stated ●`. All 8 live `specifications` rows are retired, so the view returns 0 rows until a determination is written.
workplan/pipeline-state-graph/rehearsals/D-t1-landing-r25-r24.md:90:| walkability (IDEAL-GRAPH §6) | 21 of 82 | — | 21 of 85 | 21 of 84 | **19 of 84** |
workplan/pipeline-state-graph/rehearsals/D-t1-landing-r25-r24.md:193:- **Views**: `select count(*)` from each of the 22 views, before and after, gives identical results: `v_best_practice` 0, `v_code_floor_only` 0, `v_convergence_sources` 69, `v_coverage_branch` 84, `v_coverage_jurisdiction` 27, `v_coverage_language` 20, `v_coverage_priority` 7190, `v_derived_figure_check` 0, `v_determination_provenance` 0, `v_divergence` 0, `v_evidence_authors` 53, `v_item_provenance` 0, `v_open_determination_gates` 1, `v_pending` 0, `v_pmp_latest_walk` 0, `v_registry_duplicate_descriptions` 0, `v_root_id_conflicts` 0, `v_scan_ledger` 520, `v_source_admission` 55, `v_source_reach_all` 83, `v_unregistered_roots` 0, `v_value_independence` 1. Every view's column list is identical too. Four of the six rebuilt views return 0 rows, so their verbatim SQL, not their counts, is the proof (rule 4).
workplan/pipeline-state-graph/rehearsals/D-t1-landing-r25-r24.md:299:- Helpers: `D-t1-r24-r25_tools/` (`gates.sh`, `cmp_rebuild.py`, `summ.py`, `viewcounts.py`, `svesnap.py`, `walk.py` = IDEAL-GRAPH §6 lines 606–633).
workplan/pipeline-state-graph/rehearsals/G-r18-lens.md:28:- **The repo already has four `v_coverage_*` views** (`_jurisdiction`, `_language`, `_branch`, `_priority`); the ideal's name `v_coverage` would break that family and the plan did not say so. I named it `v_coverage_lens`.
workplan/pipeline-state-graph/rehearsals/G-r18-lens.md:29:- **Counting rule differs from the ideal's** (`COUNT(*) AS searches` counts deferrals as searches). The three existing views count only `deferred_reason IS NULL` as a search, so `searches` here does the same and `deferred` is reported beside it. On the live table: 39 groups, `SUM(searches)` 190 + `SUM(deferred)` 1 = 191 rows.
workplan/pipeline-state-graph/rehearsals/G-r18-lens.md:30:- Grain is the ideal's (slug x jurisdiction x language x four codes) because a coarser view cannot be refined and a finer one rolls up by `SUM`. It is 4 lines. Today every one of its 39 groups has all four codes NULL (no pre-existing row says which lens it covered, and inventing that would be a research act).
