workplan/ratification-execution-register-2026-07-13.md:121:6. **NEW — STI acoustic-threshold three-way conflict, not previously tracked.** `references/bpc/sensory-environment/acoustics-speech-intelligibility-disability.md` states a flat "STI ≥0.5"; `references/bpc/sensory-environment/room-acoustic-performance.md` has already internally adjudicated to "STI ≥0.60 general / ≥0.75 DEAF-CI" (its own audit trail: RAP-C3 "✅ CONFIRMED — Tier 1 evidence, not contradicted"); `references/bpc/DEAF.md`'s third framing ("0.50 minimum / 0.60 best practice") is moot — that file is marked `FROZEN — historical archive... any skill reading this file is in error`, so it should never have been in the comparison set to begin with, per its own header. VERIFIED-BY: direct read of all four files' current content and header banners, this session. **The twist that blocks a point-fix:** all three live candidates carry the identical `PRE-REHABILITATION — RETRACTED PENDING REVERIFICATION` banner (DR-2026-05-23 cohort) — including room-acoustic-performance.md's own "confirmed" 0.75 figure. Picking a number now, even the seemingly-adjudicated one, would be exactly the premature-synthesis the retraction banner exists to prevent. **Recommended resolution:** flag this as a named item for the Phase E.2g reverification pass (the same mechanism GAP-269 uses for the corridor-width conflict), not a same-session number pick. Tracked as Q24.
